 ## Overview
-Debug Voxel Visualization renders a 3D voxel grid as individual geometric primitives (typically cubes or spheres) for each active voxel by iterating through the voxel data array and drawing a pre-loaded model at every non-transparent position [S2, unofficial]. It solves the problem of visualizing the discrete structure and spatial distribution of voxel data in a scene, distinct from surface extraction methods. It differs from [Axis-Aligned Bounding Box Geometry](1317-axis-aligned-bounding-box-geometry.md) and [Bounding Box Drawing](2733-bounding-box-drawing.md) by rendering individual voxel instances rather than aggregate bounding volumes, allowing for per-voxel inspection [S2, unofficial].
+Debug Voxel Visualization renders a 3D voxel grid as individual geometric primitives (typically cubes or spheres) for each active voxel by iterating through the voxel data array and drawing a pre-loaded model at every non-transparent position [S2, unofficial]. It solves the problem of visualizing the discrete structure and spatial distribution of voxel data in a scene, distinct from surface extraction methods [G]. It differs from [Axis-Aligned Bounding Box Geometry](1317-axis-aligned-bounding-box-geometry.md) and [Bounding Box Drawing](2733-bounding-box-drawing.md) by rendering individual voxel instances rather than aggregate bounding volumes, allowing for per-voxel inspection [S2, unofficial].
 
